---
// Cookies policy for the new site. Same address as the old site's page
// (/cookies-policy), so no redirect is needed.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalStyles from '../components/LegalStyles.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies Policy | TMG Plumbing & Heating"
  description="How TMG Plumbing & Heating Services uses cookies on its website, and how to change your cookie choices."
>
  <LegalStyles />
  <article class="legal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1>Cookies Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 26 September 2026</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what cookies are, which cookies www.tmgplumbing.ie uses and how you can control them.
      It should be read alongside our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What are cookies?</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files that a website places on your computer or phone. They let the website remember
      things, such as the choices you have made, and help us understand how the site is used. Similar technologies,
      such as your browser's local storage, work in the same way, and this policy covers them too.
    </p>

    <h2>How we ask for your consent</h2>
    <p>
      When you first visit the site, a banner asks whether you accept analytics and marketing cookies. These are
      switched off until you say yes. Strictly necessary cookies are always on, because the site cannot work
      without them. We remember your choice for six months, then ask again. You can change your mind at any time using the
      <button type="button" data-open-cookie-settings class="underline text-orange">Cookie settings</button>
      link here or at the bottom of every page.
    </p>

    <h2>The cookies we use</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Type</th><th>What it does</th><th>Provider</th><th>Consent needed?</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Strictly necessary</td>
          <td>Remembers your cookie choices (stored as <code>tmg-consent</code> in your browser) and lets our enquiry
            form work and protect itself from spam.</td>
          <td>TMG Plumbing &amp; Heating; Zoho (enquiry form)</td>
          <td>No</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Analytics</td>
          <td>Tells us how many people visit, which pages they look at and how they found us, so we can improve the
            site. The information is grouped and does not identify you. Typical cookies are <code>_ga</code> and
            <code>_ga_*</code>, which last up to two years.</td>
          <td>Google (Google Analytics, loaded through Google Tag Manager)</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Marketing</td>
          <td>Measures whether our online adverts lead to enquiries, and may be used to show our adverts to people who
            have visited the site.</td>
          <td>Google (Google Ads) and LinkedIn (LinkedIn Insight Tag)</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Google Tag Manager, and anything it loads, only runs after you accept analytics or marketing cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changing or deleting cookies</h2>
    <p>
      You can change your choices at any time with the
      <button type="button" data-open-cookie-settings class="underline text-orange">Cookie settings</button> link.
      You can also block or delete cookies in your browser's settings. If you block strictly necessary cookies, some
      parts of the site, such as the enquiry form, may not work properly.
    </p>
    <p>
      To opt out of Google Analytics on every website, you can install Google's
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this policy, email us at
      <a href="mailto:info@tmgplumbing.ie">info@tmgplumbing.ie</a> or call 051 577 089.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
